[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    246[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    247[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// ERRORS B14 — out-of-range enum values across the FFI boundary.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    248[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ///
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    249[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// The public API has **no enum parameter** (`const uint8_t*`, `uint32_t`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    250[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// `uint16_t`), so there is no invalid-variant int to smuggle across. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    251[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// closest analogue is that every bit pattern of the two integer parameters is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    252[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// valid input: this test drives the seed over its entire domain and `len` over
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    253[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// the low/high extremes of the `u32` domain that remain in-bounds for the
